# graphify: query the graph before grepping

- This repo may have a local context graph at `graphify-out/graph.json` (built
  by graphify: tree-sitter AST, no LLM, deterministic). It is PER-CLONE and may
  be missing on your machine — cloud sandboxes without Python/uv will not have
  it. If it is missing, fall back to the maps in README.md / KNS-CONTEXT.md and
  normal grep; do not install anything on remote sandboxes.
- When present, prefer `graphify query` / `graphify path` / `graphify affected`
  over re-reading whole files — it cuts context tokens. Verify every located
  `file:line` against the actual source before editing: the graph is a hint,
  not truth.
- Never commit `graphify-out/` (gitignored per-clone artifact) and never put
  graph builds into CI.
